---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const title = "About";
const description =
  "What Just Good Games is all about.";
---

<style>
  p {
    font-size: larger;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
</style>

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <div>
    <h1 class="text-2xl text-center md:text-5xl font-heading">About.</h1>
    <hr class="bg-accent-400 h-1 border-0 my-4 shadow-[2px_2px_0px_rgba(0,0,0,1)]" />
    <div class="flex flex-col max-w-post-100 mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-3xl text-center font-heading mt-4">What is Just Good Games?</h2>
      <div class="font-body font-semibold">
        <p>
          I love video games. I grew up playing mostly PC games in the 2000s and 2010s, reading gaming magazines like PC PowerPlay and grappling with a young, wild internet. Some of my favourite games are:
        </p>
        <ul class="italic text-xl list-inside list-disc mb-4">
          <li>Deus Ex</li>
          <li>Planescape: Torment</li>
          <li>Vampire: The Masquerade - Bloodlines</li>
          <li>Fallout: New Vegas</li>
          <li>Resident Evil</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Over the years, I've become increasingly interested in the indie gaming scene. I am regularly on the frontlines, scouring Steam's new releases page, looking for hidden gems like a crack addict. 
          With more and more games being released with every passing month, curation has become a major problem for online storefronts like Steam and Itch.io. 
          The goal of Just Good Games is to be an informative, highly opinionated outlet that promotes and escalates lesser-known games that are worth playing. Fighting back against the tidal wave of low-effort asset flips and AI slop.
        </p>
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-3xl text-center font-heading">Artifical Intelligence (AI) Policy</h2>
      <div class="font-body font-semibold">
        <p>
          AI is a powerful tool that, like most powerful tools, can be seriously misused. I prefer to take a nuanced approach rather than be firmly anti-AI or pro-AI. 
          Just Good Games will consider every game by its own merits on a case by case basis, taking into account:
        </p>
        <ol class="italic text-xl list-inside list-decimal mb-4">
          <li>Originality - was AI used to blatantly clone an existing game or its assets</li>
          <li>Human Impact - was AI used to uplift human created work or did it replace humans</li>
          <li>Implementation - was AI used to generate artwork, code, music, promotional material, voice lines and/or dynamic content</li>
        </ol>
        <p>
          In the spirit of disclosure, the AI tool Claude Code was used to assist with the backend functionality of this blog. 
          The agent completed tasks such as bug fixing, migrating/upgrading the tech stack, fixing schema and optimising SEO. 
          Reviews, round-ups and articles are typed out by hand and edited by eye. So there will probably be a lot of mistakes, and that's a good thing.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
